; Virtual pet
; Author: Achut Reddy <achut@sun.com>
;
; Virtual pet, like the currently popular "Tamagotchi" children's toys.
; The virtual pet must constantly be fed.  As long as it has sufficient food,
; it shows a happy face, and a full belly.  When it runs out, it shows a
; sad face and a slim profile.  You can then pause the machine to give it
; more food.  It will then return to a happy face until it runs out again.
;
; The last 4 lines (28-31) of store are used as the graphical display area.
; Two images are always shown there:  a full length image, and a facial
; close-up.  Both are indicators of the current "mood" of the virtual
; pet, which depends solely on the amount food it has available.
; The virtual pet has a voracious appetite; it consumes about 100 units
; of food every second.  The initial food supply is 1000, which will
; last about 10 seconds.  After the food runs out, the images change to
; sad/hungry, and it loops endlessly waiting for food.  The virtual pet can
; be fed by entering a number of food units into line 22, by temporarily
; putting the machine into Manual mode, and keying in a value. Then,
; when the program is continued, the images change to happy/full, and the
; virtual pet continues to thrive.
;
; Happy image:
;
; 28	--*-*--
; 29	-------
; 30	-*---*-
; 31	--***--
;
; Sad image:
;
; 28	--*-*--
; 29	-------
; 30	--***--
; 31	-*---*-
;
; Full image:
;
; 28	--*---
; 29	-***--
; 30	-*-*--
; 31	--*---
;
; Empty stomach image:
;
; 28	--*---
; 29	-***--
; 30	--*---
; 31	-*-*--

0    NUM 0         ; Zero word, also used as the indirect jump target for restarting at line 1.
1    LDN 22        ; ACC = -foodSupply.
2    SUB 27        ; ACC = foodSupply - 1: consume one unit of food.
3    STO 25        ; Save the decremented food value in scratch line 25.
4    LDN 25        ; ACC = updated foodSupply.
5    STO 22        ; Store the new food value back to line 22.
6    CMP           ; If food is negative, skip the next line.
7    JMP 0         ; Food still available: branch via line 0 back to line 1 and keep running.
8    LDN 23        ; ACC = -happy/full image word.
9    STO 31        ; Write it to display line 31.
10   LDN 24        ; ACC = -happy/full companion image word.
11   STO 30        ; Write it to display line 30.
12   LDN 0         ; ACC = 0.
13   STO 22        ; Reset food supply to 0 while waiting to be fed again.
14   LDN 22        ; ACC = -foodSupply.
15   CMP           ; If still negative, skip the next line.
16   JRP 26        ; Relative branch by -3 to line 14: wait here until line 22 is changed manually.
17   LDN 23        ; ACC = -happy/full image word.
18   STO 30        ; Restore one display line for the fed/happy state.
19   LDN 24        ; ACC = -happy/full companion image word.
20   STO 31        ; Restore the other display line.
21   JMP 0         ; Branch via line 0 back to the main feeding loop.
22   NUM 1000      ; Food supply counter. The user can increase this manually to feed the pet.
23   NUM -35651904 ; Encoded image word used for one happy/full display line.
24   NUM -29360256 ; Encoded image word used for the other happy/full display line.
25   NUM 0         ; Scratch line holding the decremented food value.
26   NUM -3        ; Relative branch offset used by line 16 to loop back to line 14.
27   NUM -1        ; Constant -1 for decrementing the food supply.
28   NUM 20971648  ; Static display data for the pet graphics.
29   NUM 448       ; Static display data for the pet graphics.
30   NUM 35651904  ; Display line rewritten to show mood/fullness.
31   NUM 29360256  ; Display line rewritten to show mood/fullness.
